{"task":"transcribe","language":"english","duration":40.959999084472656,"text":"The myth says Zeus released two eagles from the two ends of the earth and that they met exactly here. That is why Delphi was called the Umphilis, the navel of the world. This was the most famous oracle in the ancient world. Whole cities sent representatives to ask whether they should go to war, found a colony, or change their laws, and they queued for it. The Pythia sat on a tripod inside the temple and spoke, and priests wrote down her words. The answers were often ambiguous, meaning they could be read two ways, and that was useful to everybody. Two sentences were written on the temple wall and have lasted ever since. Know thyself, and nothing in excess.","words":[{"word":"The","start":0,"end":0.4000000059604645},{"word":"myth","start":0.4000000059604645,"end":0.6800000071525574},{"word":"says","start":0.6800000071525574,"end":1.059999942779541},{"word":"Zeus","start":1.059999942779541,"end":1.5199999809265137},{"word":"released","start":1.5199999809265137,"end":1.9600000381469727},{"word":"two","start":1.9600000381469727,"end":2.4200000762939453},{"word":"eagles","start":2.4200000762939453,"end":2.619999885559082},{"word":"from","start":2.619999885559082,"end":2.880000114440918},{"word":"the","start":2.880000114440918,"end":3.059999942779541},{"word":"two","start":3.059999942779541,"end":3.5399999618530273},{"word":"ends","start":3.5399999618530273,"end":3.5399999618530273},{"word":"of","start":3.5399999618530273,"end":3.700000047683716},{"word":"the","start":3.700000047683716,"end":3.9800000190734863},{"word":"earth","start":3.9800000190734863,"end":4},{"word":"and","start":4,"end":4.260000228881836},{"word":"that","start":4.260000228881836,"end":4.420000076293945},{"word":"they","start":4.420000076293945,"end":4.579999923706055},{"word":"met","start":4.579999923706055,"end":4.860000133514404},{"word":"exactly","start":4.860000133514404,"end":5.340000152587891},{"word":"here","start":